# Match PLL Compensation Clock, held out of the main flow.
#
#   include this file to try it:
#       set_global_assignment -name SOURCE_TCL_SCRIPT_FILE ... (see below)
#   or paste the two assignments into the revision QSF for one build.
#
# Why it exists
# -------------
# Two builds in a row report:
#
#   Warning (177007): PLL(s) placed in location FRACTIONALPLL_X54_Y38_N0 /
#   FRACTIONALPLL_X0_Y1_N0 do not have a PLL clock to compensate specified -
#   the Fitter will attempt to compensate all PLL clocks
#
# Those two locations are U_system_pll and U_fx3_pll. The AD9361 LVDS PLL is
# NOT among them, which is the whole reason this is safe to try: the
# source-synchronous receive interface is not in scope. Do not extend these
# assignments to i_altlvds_rx without a hardware RX validation plan.
#
# What it is expected to do, and what it is not
# ---------------------------------------------
# Naming a compensated output fixes the phase reference for that output's
# clock network instead of letting the fitter compensate all of them. It is
# NOT expected to fix the hold path that currently limits this design
# (fifo_writer|meta_data -> RX metadata M10K input register, skew +0.38 to
# +0.50 ns): both ends of that path are in the AD9361 clock family, and
# intra-domain skew comes from placement and local clock topology, not from
# which PLL output carries the compensation reference.
#
# Treat a timing change here as a side effect worth measuring, not as the
# mechanism. The reason to set it at all is that an unstated compensation
# target leaves a fitter choice undocumented.
#
# Both PLLs are altera_pll with a single output each, so the target node is
# unambiguous. Node names taken from a fitted netlist, not assumed:
#
#   U_system_pll|altera_pll_i|general[0].gpll~PLL_OUTPUT_COUNTER|divclk
#   U_fx3_pll|altera_pll_i|general[0].gpll~PLL_OUTPUT_COUNTER|divclk
#
# How to judge the result
# -----------------------
# Same seed, everything else unchanged. Compare:
#   - warning 177007 gone
#   - hold WNS and the identity of the worst hold path
#   - setup WNS
#   - clock skew on the metadata M10K path specifically
#   - report_clock_transfers and report_exceptions unchanged
# Then repeat across the seed set before believing any improvement.

# MATCH_PLL_COMPENSATION_CLOCK, not PLL_COMPENSATE. Both names exist --
# get_all_assignment_names lists PLL_COMPENSATE, PLL_COMPENSATION_MODE and
# MATCH_PLL_COMPENSATION_CLOCK -- and this is the one that answers 177007.
# Confirmed against the tool rather than assumed, after the DCFIFO episode
# where constraints parsed cleanly and bound to nothing.
set_instance_assignment -name MATCH_PLL_COMPENSATION_CLOCK \
    -to "U_system_pll|altera_pll_i|general[0].gpll~PLL_OUTPUT_COUNTER|divclk"

set_instance_assignment -name MATCH_PLL_COMPENSATION_CLOCK \
    -to "U_fx3_pll|altera_pll_i|general[0].gpll~PLL_OUTPUT_COUNTER|divclk"
